# Maps and exact node relations for the compressed Fi23 program

At every shared node and inverse node we retain an explicit numerical table;
single-use multiplication nodes are compositions. This keeps the original
286-node program compressed. Its endpoints are the unchanged `liftA` and
`liftB` tables, not new coordinates. The relations are certified separately
and interpreted in the genuine Fi23 carrier.

Source: GLS3 Table 5.3u, ATLAS F23G1-p31671B0, and
`GeneratorLiftCertificate/source/nodes.json`. Reproduce with
`WordEvaluation/source/generate.py`; numerical discovery is not proof.
-/

